       "reasons": [
        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/gq990gn6753.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "Pencil, read from the lower (180-degree) panel. A run of figures without separators, written close to the edge of the paper. The closing 2 and 3 are plain, so the year is 1923, and the run opens with a narrow 1 followed by a figure with a closed head, most likely 14 though 19 is possible. Between them stand two upright strokes joined by a short bar at mid height, which read either as a single open 4 (14.4.23) or as two figures, 11 (14.11.23) or 17 (no month). I cannot settle the middle group from this scan, so only the year is recorded. The roll number comes from region 2, which carries 375 alone, the 7 there crossed and carried on a long top bar."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
